Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Add=20prepaid=20=E2=82=B9=20wallet=20billing=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?behind=20an=20admin=20kill=20switch?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A second funding rail alongside plan quotas and unit credits. A workspace
on wallet billing recharges a rupee balance and every AI generation is
deducted at the real provider cost plus the platform fee.

Which rail a workspace uses is `tenants.billingMode` (quota | wallet), and
the `wallet` platform feature switch is a hard override: with it off every
workspace uses the quota rail regardless of its own setting, so the switch
is a true kill switch and needs no migration. Default is quota for
everyone, so nothing changes until an admin turns it on.

- Wallet: `wallet_balances` + append-only `wallet_ledger` in paise +
  singleton `wallet_settings`. The ledger records the APPLIED delta and the
  balance floors at zero, so SUM(ledger) always equals the balance.
- GST is exclusive everywhere in-app. It is added once, when the Razorpay
  order is created (₹1,000 top-up → ₹1,180 charged → ₹1,000 credited), and
  verification trusts the order's own notes for the split rather than
  current settings. Idempotent per order id.
- Generations reserve an estimate before the provider call, then settle to
  the real cost from the same engine that powers the Actual Cost Report.
  A model with no catalog price is charged the admin display rate and
  flagged `estimated`; adding its price collects the difference. A computed
  cost of zero counts as unknown, so nothing is ever generated for free.
- Background jobs persist their reservation (id, paise, units) so runners,
  cancels and sweeps settle or refund work that outlived the request. A
  scene added during storyboard review folds into the job's totals.
- Admin: wallet settings and a needs-pricing list on the AI tab, per-tenant
  billing mode and manual top-ups on the Tenants tab, all audited.
- Tenant: balance in the app chrome, recharge on the Billing page showing
  base amounts with the GST added at checkout spelled out, and a clear
  "Recharge to continue" 402 when the balance can't cover a generation.

